---
title: Slamhaus
description: Build static sites and interactive browser applications with Markdown and C++.
---
# Slamhaus

Slamhaus is a command-line static-site compiler for game developers. Write
ordinary GitHub Flavored Markdown, add typed UI declarations when needed, and
embed C++ that Slamhaus compiles to WebAssembly.

[View examples](examples.md)

The project emits no JavaScript for static pages and requires no handwritten
JavaScript for supported interaction.

## A small language

Pages use `.md` when they should remain portable and `.slam` when they need
Slam UI or executable code. Site configuration lives in `slamhaus.yaml`.

```slam-ui
Number Left("Left", value: 2);
Number Right("Right", value: 3);
Button Calculate("Add") => Add(Left, Right) -> Result;
Output Result("Ready");
```

The complete working version is on the [WebAssembly page](wasm.slam).

```cpp wasm
auto Add(int32 A, int32 B) -> int32 {
  return A + B;
}
```

## Start a project

```sh
slamhaus init my-site
cd my-site
slamhaus check --strict
slamhaus build
slamhaus serve
```
